{"id": "sfmta-service-contracts-outlive-their-bids", "title": "Muni’s towing and paratransit contracts outgrew their bids: $290 million added", "seconds": 130.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.024, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "0fd4d2b5f5fae696", "words": 416, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["timeline[0]", "actors[2]"], "text": "Since 2004, one firm has towed San Francisco’s illegally parked cars:", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.15, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "TEGSCO, LLC", "kicker": "San Francisco AutoReturn", "sub": "towing contractor since 2004"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.44, 0.8, 1.59, 1.85, 2.14, 2.3, 2.65, 2.84, 3.47, 3.97, 4.27]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["timeline[0]", "actors[2]"], "text": "AutoReturn, now TEGSCO.", "t0": 5.15, "t1": 7.04, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "TEGSCO, LLC", "kicker": "San Francisco AutoReturn", "sub": "towing contractor since 2004"}, "wt": [0.04, 1.07, 1.3]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["timeline[1]", "actors[3]", "story[0]"], "text": "Since 2010, Transdev has run paratransit rides for people who cannot use buses.", "t0": 7.16, "t1": 11.25, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "van", "label": "Transdev Services, Inc.", "sub": "paratransit broker since 2010"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.52, 0.93, 1.42, 1.53, 1.72, 2.3, 2.56, 2.71, 2.98, 3.1, 3.4, 3.57]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 11.37, "t1": 12.95, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in the Board’s own record. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.28, 0.36, 0.92, 1.09, 1.16]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "Both were bid in 2015, for ten years at most.", "t0": 13.07, "t1": 15.63, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Both bid in 2015", "sub": "for 10 years at most"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.35, 0.55, 0.63, 0.9, 1.53, 1.68, 1.84, 2.04, 2.12]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["amount", "story[2]"], "text": "How much have amendments added to the two since?", "t0": 15.75, "t1": 18.15, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Towing and paratransit", "kicker": "Amended again and again", "sub": "2016 to February 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.34, 0.49, 0.97, 1.2, 1.31, 1.41, 1.6]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "story[2]"], "text": "289,600,468 dollars, in ceilings, not spending.", "t0": 18.15, "t1": 21.86, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$289,600,468", "label": "added by amendment, towing and paratransit", "sub": "contract ceilings, not spending"}, "emph": ["289,600,468"], "wt": [0.04, 0.31, 0.46, 0.71, 1.15, 1.39, 1.63, 1.91, 2.28, 2.41, 3.08, 3.27]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The 2015 towing request drew three bids; TEGSCO scored highest.", "t0": 22.48, "t1": 26.52, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "btow", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst · 28 January 2026", "text": "the incumbent provider since 2004, was the highest-scoring proposer out of three bids", "mark": "three bids"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.36, 0.75, 1.07, 1.49, 1.69, 1.92, 2.71, 3.24, 3.55]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]", "timeline[11]"], "text": "Approved in 2016 at 65.4 million dollars, it reached 158.8 million.", "t0": 26.64, "t1": 31.92, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["approved, March 2016", "$65.4 million"], "b": ["tenth amendment, February 2026", "$158.8 million"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["158.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.48, 0.75, 1.25, 1.35, 1.9, 2.12, 2.33, 2.6, 3.04, 3.21, 3.51, 3.71, 3.97, 4.43, 4.68, 4.91]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]", "timeline[11]"], "text": "It now runs to June 2027, past the ten years the bid contemplated.", "t0": 32.04, "t1": 35.6, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2016-04-01", "to": "2027-06-30", "days": null, "fromLab": "towing contract begins", "toLab": "tenth amendment ends", "kicker": "beyond the initially contemplated 10-year term"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.3, 0.52, 0.65, 0.86, 1.08, 1.76, 2.04, 2.15, 2.38, 2.62, 2.72, 2.92]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "One amendment number was used twice, “due to administrative error”.", "t0": 35.72, "t1": 38.9, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Due to administrative error, this was also labeled as the First Amendment.", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, footnote 1"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.59, 0.86, 1.03, 1.25, 1.77, 2.08, 2.2, 2.81]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "notEstablished[1]", "innocent[4]"], "text": "By January 2026, the work had not gone back out to bid.", "t0": 39.02, "t1": 42.24, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "$829,400 a month", "kicker": "the management fee", "sub": "a new request was expected in early 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.64, 0.89, 1.6, 1.76, 1.95, 2.08, 2.24, 2.42, 2.62, 2.77, 2.87]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "The 2015 paratransit request drew a single respondent, Transdev.", "t0": 42.46, "t1": 46.24, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bpar", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst · 11 February 2026", "text": "following a competitive bid process where Transdev was the sole respondent", "mark": "sole respondent"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.41, 0.82, 1.4, 1.8, 2.05, 2.13, 2.41, 3.03]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[1]", "timeline[12]"], "text": "Approved in 2016 at 142.9 million dollars, it now stands at 339.1 million.", "t0": 46.36, "t1": 53.09, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "The paratransit contract ceiling", "rows": [["approved, June 2016", "$142,902,104"], ["sixth amendment, 2021", "$308,271,023"], ["tenth amendment, February 2026", "$339,102,572"]]}, "emph": ["339.1 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.44, 0.68, 1.1, 1.22, 1.39, 1.66, 2.22, 2.53, 2.8, 3.13, 3.89, 4.06, 4.25, 4.57, 4.7, 4.98, 5.26, 5.79, 6.11, 6.31]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[2]"], "text": "That makes 12 years in all, beyond the ten-year term the request advertised.", "t0": 53.21, "t1": 56.81, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "beyond the 10-year term advertised in the 2015 Request for Proposals", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, 11 February 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.42, 0.73, 0.98, 1.11, 1.48, 1.76, 1.87, 2.22, 2.44, 2.56, 2.92]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "With one bid, there was no market price to compare.", "t0": 56.93, "t1": 59.28, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "van", "label": "One bid", "sub": "no market price to compare"}, "emph": ["one bid"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.35, 0.9, 1.08, 1.19, 1.32, 1.58, 1.8, 1.9]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]", "timeline[5]"], "text": "The towing option began 1 April 2021; the Board approved it on 23 April, retroactively.", "t0": 59.5, "t1": 65.3, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Towing option, from 1 April 2021", "kicker": "Board File 21-0175", "sub": "approved 23 April 2021"}, "emph": ["retroactively"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.39, 0.66, 0.98, 1.16, 1.53, 1.82, 3.02, 3.17, 3.4, 3.74, 3.85, 3.96, 4.45, 5.0]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[3]"], "text": "The 2019 diesel contract is titled retroactive, but the old one was extended for Board review.", "t0": 65.42, "t1": 70.5, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Diesel contract, titled retroactive", "kicker": "Board File 19-0334", "sub": "old contract extended through May 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.39, 0.74, 1.02, 1.48, 1.6, 1.96, 2.97, 3.14, 3.26, 3.46, 3.74, 3.92, 4.32, 4.45, 4.69]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "The files do not say why the towing option came late.", "t0": 70.62, "t1": 72.77, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "When a renewal reaches the Board after its term has begun, the Board votes on work already under way.", "kicker": "A renewal"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.46, 0.6, 0.77, 0.94, 1.09, 1.2, 1.47, 1.74, 1.93]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "The diesel contract shows the other path: one proposer in 2015, two in 2019.", "t0": 72.99, "t1": 77.81, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Bidders for the City’s renewable diesel", "rows": [["2015", "one responsive proposer"], ["2019", "two proposals"], ["2025", "four bids"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.41, 0.82, 1.03, 1.14, 1.34, 2.09, 2.29, 2.78, 2.88, 3.14, 3.83, 4.04, 4.12, 4.36]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[5]"], "text": "Golden Gate Petroleum won with a markup of $0.12 a gallon, against $0.40.", "t0": 77.93, "t1": 81.92, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Golden Gate Petroleum", "$0.12 a gallon"], "b": ["the other proposal", "$0.40"], "kicker": "markup over the published rack price, 2019", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.52, 1.08, 1.26, 1.42, 1.48, 1.85, 1.95, 2.23, 2.44, 2.49, 2.97, 3.29, 3.56]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[5]", "links[3]"], "text": "Four amendments took it from 45 million dollars to 108.6 million.", "t0": 82.04, "t1": 86.68, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$108.6 million", "label": "the 2019 diesel contract, after four amendments", "sub": "from $45 million; SFMTA made 77.4 percent of the purchases"}, "emph": ["108.6 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.71, 0.92, 1.02, 1.23, 1.79, 2.12, 2.86, 3.06, 3.23, 3.58, 3.75, 4.01, 4.27]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "established[5]", "timeline[10]"], "text": "SFMTA buys 77.4 percent of it. Rebid in 2025, it drew four bids.", "t0": 86.8, "t1": 92.03, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Rebid, 2025", "kicker": "four bids", "sub": "Golden Gate Petroleum lowest, up to $195.0 million"}, "emph": ["four bids"], "wt": [0.0, 0.71, 0.94, 1.52, 1.76, 1.96, 2.25, 2.35, 2.98, 3.36, 3.46, 3.73, 4.34, 4.43, 4.62, 4.83]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "SFMTA’s own fuel data covers one year, 2018 to 2019, with no prices.", "t0": 92.15, "t1": 97.01, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "MTA Fuel Usage", "kicker": "DataSF nz48-2k5q", "sub": "682 deliveries, July 2018 to June 2019, no prices"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.99, 1.2, 1.43, 1.67, 1.97, 2.14, 2.37, 2.67, 3.06, 3.14, 3.41, 3.98, 4.18, 4.32]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[8]"], "text": "Michelin’s tire lease reached 9,995,000 dollars. Its next bid failed the requirements.", "t0": 97.23, "t1": 101.63, "shot": "record-8-Bus tires · $9,995,000", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bd25a", "text": "Bus tires · $9,995,000", "mark": "Bus tires · $9,995,000", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.47, 0.74, 0.96, 1.18, 1.39, 1.57, 1.85, 2.67, 2.9, 3.12, 3.38, 3.61, 3.71]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[8]"], "text": "The City then chose Michelin without another competition.", "t0": 101.75, "t1": 104.1, "shot": "record-8-File 23-0207", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bd25a", "text": "File 23-0207", "mark": "File 23-0207", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.38, 0.56, 0.85, 1.21, 1.48, 1.74]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[7]", "innocent[5]"], "text": "SFMTA amends about as often as the City: 38 percent of money files, against 34.", "t0": 104.32, "t1": 109.5, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["SFMTA", "38%"], "b": ["citywide", "34%"], "kicker": "amendments among money files at the Board, 2014-2026", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.8, 1.14, 1.34, 1.47, 1.76, 1.86, 1.98, 2.71, 3.18, 3.51, 3.61, 3.84, 4.24, 4.55]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "innocent[1]"], "text": "Federal law requires paratransit; State law caps towing fees at cost.", "t0": 109.62, "t1": 113.38, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Federal and State rules", "sub": "paratransit required since 1990; towing fees capped at cost"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.6, 0.98, 1.97, 2.27, 2.45, 2.72, 3.0, 3.21, 3.29]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["innocent[2]", "innocent[4]"], "text": "The pandemic delayed new bids, and new solicitations are planned.", "t0": 113.5, "t1": 116.38, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "New solicitations", "sub": "towing expected early 2026; paratransit Spring or Winter 2027"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.54, 0.88, 1.03, 1.33, 1.48, 1.66, 2.34, 2.45]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[3]", "notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Nothing here says any contractor was paid more than the work cost.", "t0": 116.5, "t1": 119.34, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Why the 2015 requests drew three bids and one", "Whether the costs reimbursed to Transdev were audited", "That any contractor was paid more than the work cost"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.51, 0.8, 0.99, 1.45, 1.57, 1.77, 1.92, 2.05, 2.14, 2.37]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The 2015 request files, and why others did not bid.", "t0": 119.46, "t1": 123.47, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The 2015 towing request file: plan holders, proposals and scores"}, {"who": "", "what": "The 2015 paratransit request file: why Transdev was the only respondent"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.36, 0.68, 1.17, 1.32, 1.59, 1.94, 2.3, 2.72, 2.84, 3.04, 3.37, 3.53, 3.71]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "defense[0]"], "text": "Every increase went to the Board, and its analyst recommended approving both.", "t0": 123.59, "t1": 127.35, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.64, 0.83, 0.92, 1.02, 1.7, 1.88, 2.03, 2.42, 2.98, 3.36]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 127.47, "t1": 129.38, "shot": "b29", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.34, 0.44, 0.5, 1.04, 1.23, 1.32]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Two contracts", "lead1": "Lead 1 · towing", "lead2": "Lead 2 · one bidder", "lead3": "Lead 3 · approved after the start", "lead4": "Lead 4 · diesel, rebid", "close": "Where it stands", "record": "The public record"}, "look": "map", "hook": "person"}